  65:../src/usb.c  **** /*
  66:../src/usb.c  ****  * Since we use micro A_B reptacle we need ID pin to decide device/host role.
  67:../src/usb.c  ****  * integrated ID pull-up resistor used to sample the ID line for A/B device identification
  68:../src/usb.c  ****  * If the B-side of the USB cable is connected with a floating ID wire, the integrated pullup
  69:../src/usb.c  ****  * resistor detects a high ID level and the default Peripheral role is confirmed.
  70:../src/usb.c  ****  * If the A-side of the USB cable is connected with a grounded ID, the OTG_FS issues an
  71:../src/usb.c  ****  * ID line status change interrupt (CIDSCHG bit in OTG_FS_GINTSTS) for host software
  72:../src/usb.c  ****  * initialization, and automatically switches to the host role.
  73:../src/usb.c  ****  */
